  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE NATIONAL CONVERSATION FIVE (NC5) IS A  COUNTRY-WIDE GOVERNANCE RADIO-TALK SHOW TO ACHIEVE INCREASED CITIZENS ACTION TO DEMAND THEIR RIGHTS/NEEDS.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main intended impact of the project is that, Women and men (including various marginalised groups) in Tanzania (aged 25-45 years) feel confident to demand their rights, express their views freely (in person and online) and participate in meaningful and inclusive discussion during local decision-making process in relation to issues that matter to them, with a particular focus on the provision of public services (including access to water and healthcare), livelihoods, gender equality and adaptation to the impacts of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
